ADD - the simplest seed: a number in, a number out.

Language features
  - SEED_EXPORT - a plain seed you load with SEED and call with CALL
  - numeric arguments and a numeric return value
  - proves the whole position-independent load / cache / call pipeline

Try it
  SEED h%, "ADD.SED"
    PRINT CALL(h%, 40, 2)        -> 42

Build it on the machine
  grow add          # -> build/ADD.SED
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as ADD.SED, ready to use.

